<h1>ds_grid_width</h1>
<p>This function will return the width of the given grid. This value is the number of cells the grid has along the x-axis and is always an integer, as shown in the image below:</p>
<p><img alt="DS grid width" class="center" src="../../../../assets/Images/Scripting_Reference/GML/Reference/Data_Structures/ds_grid_width.png" /></p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">ds_grid_width(index);</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th><th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>index</td><td><span data-keyref="Type_ID_DS_Grid"><a target="_blank" href="ds_grid_create.htm">DS Grid</a></span></td>
<td>This index of the grid to find the width of.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">for (var i = 0; i &lt; ds_grid_width(grid); ++i)<br/>
{<br/>
    for (var j = 0; j &lt; ds_grid_height(grid); ++j)<br/>
    {<br/>
        if (ds_grid_get(grid, i, j) == 1)<br/>
        {<br/>
            instance_create_layer(i * 32, j * 32, &quot;Walls&quot;, obj_Wall);<br/>
        }<br/>
    }<br/>
}</p>
<p>The above code will loop through the DS grid indexed in the variable &quot;grid&quot; and if the value found in any specific cell is equal to 1, it will then create an instance of &quot;obj_Wall&quot; at the appropriate position within the room.</p>
<p> </p>
